============================================================
 SKEW MITIGATION SUMMARY
============================================================
 Without salting               34.6s  ->  100,852 orders
 With salting                  79.1s  ->  100,852 orders
 Speedup                       0.44x  (salting SLOWER in this dataset)
 Top-1 user share              0.02%
============================================================
 ANALYSIS:
   Salting was counterproductive — top-1 user is only 0.02% of events,
   meaning there is no real skew to mitigate. The crossJoin replicates
   the orders table 20x which adds more overhead than it saves.
   Salting is only beneficial when a single key accounts for >1-5% of rows.

